## The five defects (fix each at its single owner; state rule count before/after)
1. `runtime/host/index.ts:1888-1893` — after `publishHostDraining()` succeeds the shutdown path unconditionally waits a polling interval
   (default 1000 ms) → with the runner's 500 ms grace, roles are SIGKILLed before Spot teardown starts. Remove the wait that has no
   contract basis (§14 orders callbacks → cleanup; publication is fire-and-observe). Do NOT touch the runner grace.
2. `spots/index.ts:1102-1107` waits for the Spot collection to empty after `requestDrainClose()`, but `spot-activation-state.ts:376-378,419-421`
   refuses to start close while joined Actors remain (`canClose=false`) → SupportChat/ZoneWorld hang. HostShutdown must close scopes
   regardless of membership (§14) — implement in the Spot lifecycle owner; one close rule, no shutdown-specific bypass flag layered on top.
3. `spot-activation.ts:738-743` runs close as a detached task and `spots/index.ts:1107` observes only collection removal → a throwing
   `onClosing()` yields `Stopped` instead of `ForceStopped/TeardownFailed`. Route the close terminal (incl. error) to the shared
   shutdown owner so the outcome is observed once, at one place.
4. `host/index.ts:1918-1920` force-stop waits for the same drain with no bound; `spot-activation.ts:979-982` does not pass the host's
   remaining deadline to `invokeSpotClosing()` so `spot-closing.ts:6` 30 000 ms applies. Propagate the single host deadline (already
   owned by `shutdown({deadlineMs})`) — no new budget.
5. `host/index.ts:1781-1785` calls `setChannelWeight()` for client-only memberships; startup registers only server channels
   (`spot-node-runtime-manager.ts:360-364`) so `node-raw-mesh-backend.ts:457` rejects them and force-stop is entered (ZoneWorld
   `zoneworld.report`/`zoneworld.zones`). Publish Draining only for the memberships the local server owner actually registered — reuse that
   owner's list, do not register client memberships as fake servers.

## Verify (all required)
- `npm run build`, `npm run typecheck`, lint on touched files.
- `test/contract/nestjs-shutdown.test.js` 4/4 (the callback-failure and deadline cases must now pass without changing the assertions),
  `stream-heartbeat-shutdown`, `sample-runner-teardown`, and every contract test of the touched subsystems (spots, spot-activation, host).
- All 7 node samples individually: exit 0 and no role SIGKILLed at cleanup (TicTacToe, SupportChat, ZoneWorld were the reds), then
  `bash samples/run_samples.sh` once (aggregate exit 0), then `npm test` once (0 fail).
- If a sample still fails for a reason outside these five, root-cause it the same way (owner + spec clause) and fix it; do not leave a
  "known red".

